{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ef7e39d99b57bc5af4", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Alternating Current - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46b4"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b466e", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4606", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "An <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> current is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />A hot wire ammeter will give a reading:"}, "options": [{"id": "e6865d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>-</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4607"}, {"id": "cb36a8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4608"}, {"id": "8ba85c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4609"}, {"id": "bec38b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b460a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b460b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b4"], "question": {"text": "In an LC oscillator, if values of inductance and capacitance become twice and eight times, respectively, then the resonant frequency of oscillator becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> times its initial resonant frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "5f510b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b460c"}, {"id": "1047f6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b460d"}, {"id": "49ed04", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b460e"}, {"id": "91adde", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b460f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4610", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e46"], "question": {"text": "If wattless current flows in the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AC</mi></math> circuit, then the circuit is :"}, "options": [{"id": "b32808", "text": "Purely Resistive circuit", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4611"}, {"id": "c56bac", "text": "Purely Inductive circuit", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4612"}, {"id": "b0d0f7", "text": "LCR series circuit", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4613"}, {"id": "049617", "text": "RC series circuit only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4614"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4615", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ac"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements : one is labelled as Assertion (A) and the other is labelled as Reason (R).\nAssertion (A) : Choke coil is simply a coil having a large inductance but a small resistance. Choke coils are used with fluorescent mercury-tube fittings. If household electric power is directly connected to a mercury tube, the tube will be damaged.\nReason (R): By using the choke coil, the voltage across the tube is reduced by a factor \\(\\left(R / \\sqrt{R^2+\\omega^2 L^2}\\right)\\), where \\(\\omega\\) is frequency of the supply across resistor \\(R\\) and inductor L . If the choke coil were not used, the voltage across the resistor would be the same as the applied voltage.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "75efc0", "text": "\\((A)\\) is true but (R) is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4616"}, {"id": "ed1123", "text": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4617"}, {"id": "9cee68", "text": "(A) is false but (R) is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4618"}, {"id": "a78db6", "text": "Both \\((\\mathbf{A})\\) and \\((\\mathbf{R})\\) are true but \\((\\mathbf{R})\\) is not the correct explanation of \\((\\mathbf{A})\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4619"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b461a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4712"], "question": {"text": "In the figure shown, a circuit contains two identical resistors with resistance <math><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>&#937;</mi></math> and an inductance with <math><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>m</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>.</mo></math> An ideal battery of <math><mn>15</mn><mi>V</mi></math> is connected in the circuit. What will be the current through the battery long after the switch is closed?<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fcivwrfuzbhvhdnpjxmjyowjujddqconbickfdhhpxrioadaznl.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "954a59", "text": "<math><mn>5.5</mn><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b461b"}, {"id": "624be1", "text": "<math><mn>6</mn><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b461c"}, {"id": "f77ac3", "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b461d"}, {"id": "44247b", "text": "<math><mn>7.5</mn><mi> </mi><mi>A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b461e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b461f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b58"], "question": {"text": "In an a.c. circuit, voltage and current are given by: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>100</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>mA</mi></math> respectively. The average power dissipated in one cycle is :"}, "options": [{"id": "aa899d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4620"}, {"id": "588f35", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4621"}, {"id": "5e1582", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4622"}, {"id": "25cd72", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4623"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4624", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e94a2493707322b06e318f"], "question": {"text": "<p>An <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></math> circuit as shown in the figure is driven by a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> source generating a square wave. The output wave pattern monitored by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>O</mi></math> would look close to :</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5f0aa413-bf73-4037-8ded-082f67bcac66-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 439px; height: 164px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "7ec6b3", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F0c1da3fe-e536-48ec-b8a7-dd3e70299615-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 285px; height: 84px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4625"}, {"id": "71090c", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F31269e93-017f-47f9-96e5-a08ba380fe86-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 285px; height: 87px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4626"}, {"id": "e4cff9", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F69d15efd-559d-49e4-985e-8e6baf24c04f-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 305px; height: 77px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4627"}, {"id": "b9abe4", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fde6912b6-a1a5-4a90-ad20-aa0137841be7-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 305px; height: 89px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4628"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4629", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "An alternating current is given by $\\mathrm{I}=\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{A}} \\sin \\omega \\mathrm{t}+\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}} \\cos \\omega \\mathrm{t}$. The r.m.s current will be"}, "options": [{"id": "95c2dc", "text": "$\\frac{\\left|\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{A}}+\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}}\\right|}{\\sqrt{2}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b462a"}, {"id": "887bf3", "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{A}}^2+\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}}^2}{2}}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b462b"}, {"id": "d040f8", "text": "$\\sqrt{\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{A}}^2+\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}}^2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b462c"}, {"id": "7a5c0b", "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{A}}^2+\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{B}}^2}}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b462d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b462e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e46"], "question": {"text": "In <math><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi></math> circuit the inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math> and capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If a voltage <math><mi>V</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>314</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is applied to the circuit, the current in the circuit is given as:"}, "options": [{"id": "81d6a9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.52</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>314</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b462f"}, {"id": "66ece7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>314</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4630"}, {"id": "32cfcd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>314</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4631"}, {"id": "a41d4a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.52</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>314</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4632"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4633", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "In an ac circuit, the instantaneous current is zero, when the instantaneous voltage is maximum. In this case, the source may be connected to :\nA. pure inductor.\nB. pure capacitor.\nC. pure resistor.\nD. combination of an inductor and capacitor.\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "954c6e", "text": "A, B and C only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4634"}, {"id": "2c8025", "text": "A and B only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4635"}, {"id": "7a9a4b", "text": "B, C and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4636"}, {"id": "ce8950", "text": "A, B and D only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4637"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4638", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b4"], "question": {"text": "To increase the resonant frequency in series LCR circuit,"}, "options": [{"id": "5f9cbe", "text": "Source frequency should be increased", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4639"}, {"id": "c93090", "text": "Another resistance should be added in series with the first resistance.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b463a"}, {"id": "be1e75", "text": "Another capacitor should be added in series with the first capacitor", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b463b"}, {"id": "9a45f9", "text": "The source frequency should be decreased", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b463c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b463d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95ca"], "question": {"text": "An alternating voltage source <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>260</mn><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>628</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is connected across a pure inductor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math>. Inductive reactance in the circuit is:"}, "options": [{"id": "47e3fe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#8486;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b463e"}, {"id": "b23c33", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>&#8486;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b463f"}, {"id": "9d24ab", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8486;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4640"}, {"id": "cf000a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>318</mn><mo>&#8486;</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4641"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4642", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4712"], "question": {"text": "<p>A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>07</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> inductor and a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> resistor are connected in series to a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>&nbsp;AC&nbsp;source. The approximate current in the circuit and the phase angle between current and source voltage are respectively.</p><p>[Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi></math> as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"\"><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2dce49", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4643"}, {"id": "630afd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>88</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id":