": "2026-04-14T14:28:23.780Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:23.780Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46b2"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46b0", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4694", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e46"], "question": {"text": "<p>In the given circuit, the magnitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math> are twice that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></math>. Given that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>, the inductance of the coil is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mH</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc0db48be-69b5-4054-a042-a1a42a78fddf-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 210px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a76d72", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4695"}, {"id": "4a1774", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4696"}, {"id": "02af09", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4697"}, {"id": "238822", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4698"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b4699", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e5673b499d1e49588f8b88"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b58"], "question": {"text": "An inductor of reactance $100 \\Omega$, a capacitor of reactance $50 \\Omega$, and a resistor of resistance $50 \\Omega$ are connected in series with an AC source of 10 V , 50 Hz. Average power dissipated by the circuit is ________ W."}, "options": [{"id": "2dfcfb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b469a"}, {"id": "0c3f16", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b469b"}, {"id": "617e2a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b469c"}, {"id": "e56835", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b469d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b469e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b5b"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa022"], "question": {"text": "A series LCR circuit with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi>mH</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>π</mi></mfrac><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>, is connected across an AC source of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Hz</mi></math> supply. The power factor of the circuit would be ____."}, "options": [{"id": "86da69", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b469f"}, {"id": "12edbd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a0"}, {"id": "35e312", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a1"}, {"id": "c4a576", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52e6"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52ac"], "question": {"text": "<p>An ideal transformer with purely resistive load operates at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kV</mi></math> on the primary side. It supplies electrical energy to a number of nearby houses at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The average rate of energy consumption in the houses served by the transformer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kW</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The value of resistive load <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></math> required in the secondary circuit will be<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_________m&#937;</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "8d2db0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a4"}, {"id": "321f8a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a5"}, {"id": "3d9490", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a6"}, {"id": "96e1c6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae7"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52b4"], "question": {"text": "In a series LCR resonant circuit, the quality factor is measured as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>. If the inductance is increased by two fold and resistance is decreased by two fold, then the quality factor after this change will be _______"}, "options": [{"id": "090dc1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f075dcf815cd79b46a9"}, {"id": "b83940", "text": "", "i